1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:40,344 --> 00:01:41,664
The Roadmap to End War and Disease This isn't a protest.

8
00:01:41,744 --> 00:01:42,244
It's a recipe.

9
00:01:42,804 --> 00:01:45,924
Step one, collect papers from rich humans (using greed).

10
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:50,784
Step two, get two hundred and eighty million humans to click a button (using

11
00:01:50,784 --> 00:01:54,664
paid referral bonuses, because your species won't save itself for free).

12
00:01:55,324 --> 00:01:59,604
Step three, apply papers to politicians until the treaty happens (using

13
00:01:59,604 --> 00:02:01,164
the only language they understand).

14
00:02:02,124 --> 00:02:03,084
Every step has a budget,

15
00:02:08,924 --> 00:02:09,604
a timeline, and a contingency plan for the fact that you're you. This isn't a protest.

16
00:02:09,604 --> 00:02:10,104
It's a recipe.

17
00:02:10,624 --> 00:02:15,564
Like making bread, except instead of bread it's curing diseases, and instead

18
00:02:15,564 --> 00:02:17,624
of yeast it's (legal) bribes.

19
00:02:18,464 --> 00:02:19,824
High-Level Strategy:

20
00:02:19,904 --> 00:02:22,784
The Three-Step Recipe for Not Dying.

21
00:02:23,624 --> 00:02:25,004
Humans love steps.

22
00:02:25,104 --> 00:02:26,074
You put them on everything.

23
00:02:27,064 --> 00:02:27,564
Step one:

24
00:02:27,844 --> 00:02:28,344
Breathe.

25
00:02:28,584 --> 00:02:29,124
Step two:

26
00:02:29,444 --> 00:02:30,084
Keep breathing.

27
00:02:30,604 --> 00:02:31,144
Step three:

28
00:02:31,604 --> 00:02:32,644
Try not to die.

29
00:02:33,204 --> 00:02:35,624
You're very methodical about staying alive.

30
00:02:36,344 --> 00:02:40,564
That makes it curious that you spend six hundred and four times more on

31
00:02:40,564 --> 00:02:43,424
weapons than testing which medicines work.

32
00:02:44,244 --> 00:02:49,164
Here's your three-step algorithm for fixing this adorable contradiction:

33
00:02:49,864 --> 00:02:50,364
Step One:

34
00:02:50,864 --> 00:02:52,524
Collect Papers from Rich People.

35
00:02:53,084 --> 00:02:57,604
You convince wealthy humans to give you a large pile of papers by promising

36
00:02:57,604 --> 00:03:00,964
them returns that make explosion manufacturers nervous.

37
00:03:01,624 --> 00:03:05,844
This works because rich people are excellent at counting papers but terrible

38
00:03:05,844 --> 00:03:07,864
at not wanting more papers.

39
00:03:08,424 --> 00:03:09,884
The pitch is simple:

40
00:03:09,984 --> 00:03:12,704
"Give us papers now, get more papers forever,

41
00:03:13,444 --> 00:03:16,604
also maybe don't die from preventable diseases."

42
00:03:17,124 --> 00:03:21,864
Even humans who think vaccines cause five G can understand "more papers

43
00:03:21,864 --> 00:03:22,424
good.".

44
00:03:23,444 --> 00:03:23,944
Step Two:

45
00:03:24,284 --> 00:03:26,224
Tell Humans the Referendum Exists.

46
00:03:27,224 --> 00:03:31,384
Use some papers to launch a global marketing campaign so two hundred and

47
00:03:31,384 --> 00:03:35,144
eighty million people learn there's a referendum and vote on it.

48
00:03:35,864 --> 00:03:39,364
This achieves more than most political movements involving shouting.

49
00:03:40,064 --> 00:03:42,424
The referendum isn't a simple yes/no.

50
00:03:43,184 --> 00:03:47,784
Each voter gets a wishocratic slider to set their preferred allocation between

51
00:03:47,784 --> 00:03:50,804
military spending and clinical trials. The results are aggregated to determine humanity's collective preferred split.

52
00:03:50,804 --> 00:03:52,524
It's a species-wide budget meeting.

53
00:03:53,604 --> 00:03:56,294
You'd think the outcome would be obvious.

54
00:03:56,384 --> 00:04:00,504
But humans once thought the sun went around Earth, so you have to ask.

55
00:04:01,544 --> 00:04:04,484
This creates what's called "political pressure."

56
00:04:04,544 --> 00:04:08,544
That's when politicians realize that voters exist and some of them have

57
00:04:08,544 --> 00:04:09,044
opinions.

58
00:04:09,904 --> 00:04:10,924
Step Three:

59
00:04:11,044 --> 00:04:14,674
Apply Papers to Politicians Until Treaty Happens.

60
00:04:14,784 --> 00:04:18,564
Deploy the remaining papers to convince politicians that supporting the

61
00:04:18,564 --> 00:04:21,524
treaty is the only way to remain employed.

62
00:04:22,064 --> 00:04:22,864
The treaty passes.

63
00:04:23,664 --> 00:04:28,904
Twenty-seven point two billion dollars per year flows from murder to medicine.

64
00:04:29,444 --> 00:04:29,944
Forever.

65
00:04:30,304 --> 00:04:31,794
Or until the sun explodes.

66
00:04:32,364 --> 00:04:34,744
Whichever happens first (probably the sun).

67
00:04:35,684 --> 00:04:38,204
The Sacred (Legal) Bribery Sequence.

68
00:04:39,204 --> 00:04:41,324
Humans respond to papers.

69
00:04:41,884 --> 00:04:44,144
This is your most important discovery about Earth.

70
00:04:44,684 --> 00:04:46,874
You tried appealing to morality (failed).

71
00:04:47,604 --> 00:04:50,144
You tried appealing to logic (failed harder).

72
00:04:50,604 --> 00:04:51,104
But papers?

73
00:04:51,804 --> 00:04:53,484
Papers work every time.

74
00:04:54,084 --> 00:04:58,084
Here's the precise order for distributing papers to specific categories

75
00:04:58,084 --> 00:04:59,584
